  "id": "real-07",
  "question": "Build a reactivation offer for dormant elite members and quote the projected RASK recovered.",
  "reply": "## Reactivation Offer — Dormant Elite Platino Members\n\n**Agent Stack note:** Pulled the member/network truth from `query_members` (Platino/Titanio, sorted by churnRisk), then delegated offer design to `offer-strategist`. No sandbox chart was needed here since we already had a clean 2-member target list; loyalty-definitions skill was loaded for RASK/segment thresholds.\n\n### Fixed-ASK framing\nASK on the network is fixed at 1.734M seat-km this period (network load factor 80.5%, RASK 2.66 MXN). These two members aren't idle capacity we can create — they represent **unfilled long-haul international ASK on routes they've already proven they'll pay premium yield for** (MEX-MAD RASK 3.02, MEX-JFK RASK 2.95 — both above network average). Winning them back doesn't grow ASK; it recovers load factor and yield on capacity that's flying anyway.\n\n### Who's dormant and elite\nBoth members carry `marketingSegment = \"Dormant Elite\"` and sit in **Retencion Prioritaria** (high value + high churn risk):\n\n| Member | Tier | Hub | Days since last flight | Value/Churn | RASK-at-risk | CLV | Historic routes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **CP10000006** Guadalupe González | Platino | MEX | 153 | 63 / 56.2 | **169,059 MXN** | 300,000 MXN | MEX-MAD, MEX-GRU, MEX-LAX, MEX-JFK, MEX-BOG |\n| **CP10000008** Verónica Sánchez | Platino | GDL | 175 | 60.1 / 51 | **89,269 MXN** | 315,000 MXN | MEX-MAD, MEX-BOG, MEX-LAX, MEX-JFK |\n\nCombined they carry **258,328 MXN** of RASK-at-risk — **54.1% of all RASK-at-risk across the Platino/Titanio tiers** (477,604 MXN total, per `query_members` rollup). Both are NPS detractors with declining engagement (Guadalupe: no app, 22% email open; Verónica: app installed but 30% email open, push opt-out).\n\n### Offer design (from `offer-strategist`)\n**\"Dormant Elite Reactivation Bonus\" (`reactivationBonus`):** contingent-redemption Puntos Premier bonus that only pays out if the member rebooks and flies within 30 days (60-day outreach window) — targeted at their historic high-yield international lanes (MEX-MAD, MEX-JFK, MEX-LAX, MEX-BOG). This is deliberately points-contingent, not a cash fare discount, to protect Premier-cabin yield.\n\n- **Incentive cost:** 750 MXN/member × 2 = **1,500 MXN** total\n- **Projected RASK recovered:** **77,498 MXN** combined (~30% recovery factor applied to the 258,328 MXN at-risk base — a modeled assumption from the offer playbook, not a measured outcome)\n- **ROI:** ~**51.7x** RASK recovered per peso of incentive\n- **Downside is capped:** cost only fires on actual rebooking, so if disengagement wins, exposure stays at cheap contingent cost — but the 615,000 MXN combined CLV and their Platino tier renewal remain unprotected without a successful nudge.\n\n### Channel routing\n- **Guadalupe (CP10000006):** email (opted in, predicted channel) — lead with her Premier-cabin international routes and Santander co-brand tie-in (70K MXN/12m spend).\n- **Verónica (CP10000008):** in-app/push banner (app installed, despite push opt-out) as primary, email as fallback only — her 30% email open rate makes email a weak sole channel. Reference her Bimbo corporate account and Santander spend (95K MXN/12m) for relevance.\n\n**Bottom line:** This is a 1,500 MXN bet to recover ~77,500 MXN of RASK on fixed, already-scheduled long-haul ASK (MEX-MAD/JFK/LAX/BOG) — no capacity added, just higher-yield fill on two Platino accounts holding over half the tier's churn exposure.",
  "toolCalls": [
    {
      "name": "load_skill",
      "input": {
        "skill": "loyalty-definitions"
      },
      "output": "# Club Premier Loyalty Definitions\n\nUse these definitions before interpreting network performance or member segments.\n\n## Network metrics\n\n- `ASK` (Available Seat Kilometers): fixed network capacity for the period — seats offered times distance\n  flown. Loyalty cannot change ASK; it is set by network/fleet planning. `askMillions` in the data is\n  expressed in millions of seat-km.\n- `RPK` (Revenue Passenger Kilometers): seats actually sold/flown times distance. Loyalty's job is to grow\n  RPK against the fixed ASK.\n- `Load factor`: RPK / ASK. The share of fixed capacity actually filled.\n- `RASK` (Revenue per ASK): (passenger revenue + ancillary revenue) / ASK. The headline revenue-efficiency\n  metric — it rises from higher load factor, higher yield, or more ancillary attach, never from more ASK.\n- `Yield`: passenger revenue per RPK (MXN per km flown). Reflects fare/cabin mix.\n- `Ancillary share`: ancillary revenue as a share of total (passenger + ancillary) revenue.\n\n## Fixed-ASK doctrine\n\nASK is FIXED network capacity. Loyalty programs, offers, and retention campaigns cannot add ASK — they can\nonly change how efficiently the existing ASK converts to revenue (load factor, RASK, yield, ancillary,\nCLV/retention). Never frame a loyalty recommendation as \"growing capacity\"; frame it as \"filling the fixed\nASK more profitably.\"\n\n## Club Premier tiers\n\nAscending order: `Clasico` → `Plata` → `Oro` → `Platino` → `Titanio`. Higher tiers skew toward Premier cabin,\nlonger-haul international routes, and higher award-redemption rates.\n\n## Member value and churn scoring\n\n- `valueScore` (0-100): weighted composite of CLV, trailing-12m RPK, trailing-12m passenger + ancillary\n  revenue, tier rank, and co-brand card spend. A member is high value at `valueScore >= 60`.\n- `churnRisk` (0-100): weighted composite of days since last flight, app/web login recency, flight\n  frequency (inverse), CSAT (inverse), and service-case friction. A member is high risk at\n  `churnRisk >= 50`.\n- `raskAtRiskMxn`: trailing-12m passenger + ancillary revenue weighted by `churnRisk` — the RASK exposure if\n  the member churns.\n\n## Segments\n\n- `Retencion Prioritaria`: high value AND high risk (`valueScore >= 60` and `churnRisk >= 50`). Highest\n  priority for retention offers — largest RASK-at-risk per member.\n- `Embajadores`: high value, low risk. Protect and grow; strong co-brand/upsell candidates.\n- `En Riesgo`: low value, high risk. Lower RASK exposure but still churn-prone; use low-cost retention plays.\n- `Base`: low value, low risk. Standard servicing, no special intervention needed.\n",
      "status": "completed",
      "turnIndex": 0,
      "sessionId": "wrun_01M32XAXFJ1NAAC8XJZ9RJ5CT5"
    },
